// The bank of urgent errands (lib/encargos.js): ten or more per trade and fifteen for whoever has none. An errand is
// a situation with a real deadline and two or three ways to go about it. Every number is here, in the code, and the
// outcome is rolled: nothing is left to the AI.
//   c(name, chance, prize, good, bad): chance % of making it, before the group helps or sabotages; prize in UruCoins,
//     paid only when it goes well; good and bad are what Claudia tells the group in each case.
// The texts speak to whoever got the errand ("te cayó", "llegaste"), and say nothing that takes them for a man or a
// woman.
// To add one: a new entry in its trade's list (or in ENCARGOS_GENERALES), with an id nobody else has in that list. It
// is stored by its key ("camionero/sobre-a-rivera", "general/mate-para-la-suegra"), so an id isn't renamed once it's
// been out.
// test/encargos-banco.test.mjs checks the shape of all of this, that no way is a gift or a robbery, and that no two
// errands are the same one.
const c = (nombre, chance, premio, bien, mal) => ({ nombre, chance, premio, bien, mal });

